From 09a139abca3ee8e21f508cd53b29aea1e21a54da Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: verkur46 <mohamadrezasahami1999@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:19:24 +0330
Subject: [PATCH 142/230] fix(ops): per-league sync rows carried no timestamp
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The health snapshot's SQL aliased MAX(last_synced_at) AS t while the
mapping read r.lastSyncedAt, so /api/health/sync returned per-league
rows like {"league":"bel.1"} with the date silently dropped (undefined
is omitted by JSON). Alias to the field's own name; verified live that
every league row now carries its ledger date.

🤖 Generated with Codebuff
Co-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>
---
 server/sync/sentinel.ts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/server/sync/sentinel.ts b/server/sync/sentinel.ts
index 28b0728..2836d5c 100644
--- a/server/sync/sentinel.ts
+++ b/server/sync/sentinel.ts
@@ -98,7 +98,7 @@ export function syncHealthSnapshot(db: DB, now: Date = new Date()): SyncHealthSn
   );
   const perLeague = all<LeagueSyncRow>(
     db,
-    `SELECT league, MAX(last_synced_at) AS t
+    `SELECT league, MAX(last_synced_at) AS lastSyncedAt
      FROM matches WHERE last_synced_at IS NOT NULL GROUP BY league ORDER BY league ASC`,
   );
 
